---
// Get started: how to connect the hosted playmat to claude.ai, ChatGPT and
// Claude Code, how to check it works, and how to refresh the connection
// after an update (#refresh). Every address comes from the site facts. The
// ChatGPT Plugin Directory steps show only once lib/listing.ts says TCG
// Replay is listed; until then no page mentions the Plugin Directory.
//
// The page's content stays flat (h2, p, ol and copy blocks directly in the
// docs layout's article) so the browser suite can group it by heading.
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import CopyBlock from '../../components/CopyBlock.astro';
import Prompt from '../../components/Prompt.astro';
import { site } from '../../lib/facts';
import { chatgptDirectory, chatgptPlans } from '../../lib/listing';

const check = 'What can the tcgreplay playmat do?';
---
<Docs
  title="Get started"
  description="Connect the hosted tcgreplay playmat to claude.ai, ChatGPT or Claude Code, and check it works."
>
  <h1>Get started</h1>
  <CopyBlock text={site.mcpURL} label="The playmat's address" wrap class="address" />

  <p>
    tcgreplay runs as a connector (an MCP server) for the AI assistant you already use. Add the hosted playmat at the
    address above, sign in with Google the first time it is used, and the assistant can import your games, coach you
    and show the board.
  </p>
  <p>
    You need a Google account to sign in. The hosted playmat serves a few players at once; if it is full, you can <a href="/docs/desktop">run it on your own computer</a> instead.
  </p>

  <aside class="note" id="moved" data-moved-note>
    <p><strong>Connected before?</strong> The playmat used to be at <code>tcgreplay.demo.gs</code>. If your connector still uses <code>https://tcgreplay.demo.gs/mcp</code>, remove it and add <code>{site.mcpURL}</code> instead, then sign in again.</p>
  </aside>

  <h2>claude.ai</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open <strong>Settings → Connectors</strong> and choose <strong>Add custom connector</strong>.</li>
    <li>Name it <code>tcgreplay</code> and paste the playmat's address, <code>{site.mcpURL}</code>.</li>
    <li>
      Choose <strong>Add</strong>, then <strong>Connect</strong>. Google asks you to choose an account: pick one and
      allow it to share your email address. You come back to claude.ai.
    </li>
    <li>In a chat, make sure tcgreplay is switched on in the chat's tools menu.</li>
  </ol>
  <p><strong>Check it works.</strong> Start a new chat and ask:</p>
  <Prompt text={check} />
  <p>
    Claude should list the playmat's coaching workflows, such as importing a game, reviewing it and drills. If it says
    it can't reach the playmat, open the connector in <strong>Settings → Connectors</strong> and connect it again. If a
    tool seems missing after an update, <a href="#refresh">refresh the connection</a>. See <a href="/docs/sign-in">signing in and opening the board</a> for what the sign-in looks like.
  </p>

  <h2>ChatGPT</h2>
  <p>
    Adding a custom MCP server needs ChatGPT on the web, on a {chatgptPlans} plan. On Business, a workspace admin or
    owner adds it for the workspace.
  </p>
  {chatgptDirectory.listed && (
    <>
      <p>Find {chatgptDirectory.name} in ChatGPT's Plugin Directory:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Open <strong>Plugins</strong> in ChatGPT.</li>
        <li>Search for "{chatgptDirectory.name}".</li>
        <li>Open it and choose <strong>Add</strong> (or <strong>Connect</strong>).</li>
        <li>Sign in with Google when asked, and allow it to share your email address.</li>
        <li>In a new chat, type <code>@</code> and pick {chatgptDirectory.name}.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Or add it yourself as a custom connection:</p>
    </>
  )}
  <ol>
    <li>
      In ChatGPT on the web, open <strong>Plugins</strong> (chatgpt.com/plugins), select <strong>+</strong>, then <strong>Add custom MCP server</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Name it <code>tcgreplay</code> and, under <strong>Connection</strong>, paste the playmat's address, <code>{site.mcpURL}</code>, as the <strong>Server URL</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>Leave authentication on <strong>OAuth</strong>.</li>
    <li>
      Read the warning, choose <strong>I understand and want to continue</strong>, then <strong>Create as a plugin</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Find tcgreplay in your plugins and <strong>Install</strong> it. The first time it is used, Google asks you to
      choose an account and share your email address, and you come back to ChatGPT.
    </li>
    <li>In a new chat, type <code>@</code> and pick tcgreplay.</li>
  </ol>
  <p><strong>Check it works.</strong> Start a new chat and ask:</p>
  <Prompt text={check} />
  <p>
    ChatGPT should list the playmat's coaching workflows. If it can't reach the playmat, open tcgreplay in <strong>Plugins</strong> and connect it again. If a tool seems missing after an update, <a href="#refresh">refresh the connection</a>. See <a href="/docs/sign-in">signing in and opening the board</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Claude Code</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <p>In a terminal, add the playmat:</p>
      <pre><code>{`claude mcp add --transport http tcgreplay ${site.mcpURL}`}</code></pre>
    </li>
    <li>
      Start Claude Code, type <code>/mcp</code>, choose <strong>tcgreplay</strong> and <strong>Authenticate</strong>.
      Your browser opens Google's account chooser; pick your account, then return to the terminal.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p><strong>Check it works.</strong> Ask Claude Code:</p>
  <Prompt text={check} />
  <p>
    It should list the playmat's coaching workflows. If it can't reach the playmat, run <code>/mcp</code> again and
    authenticate tcgreplay. If a tool seems missing after an update, <a href="#refresh">refresh the connection</a>. See <a href="/docs/sign-in">signing in and opening the board</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>The Claude desktop app</h2>
  <p>
    The desktop app can use the playmat running on your own computer, with no sign-in. See <a href="/docs/desktop">running it on your desktop</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="refresh">Refresh after an update</h2>
  <p>
    When tcgreplay adds or changes a tool, your assistant may keep the list it saw when you connected, so a new tool
    seems missing or an old one behaves oddly. <a href="/docs/whats-new">What's new</a> says when an update needs a
    refresh.
  </p>
  <h3>claude.ai</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Open <strong>Settings → Connectors</strong>.</li>
    <li>Remove tcgreplay.</li>
    <li>Add it again with the playmat's address, <code>{site.mcpURL}</code>, and connect.</li>
    <li>Start a new chat.</li>
  </ol>
  <h3>ChatGPT</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Open <strong>Plugins</strong> and choose tcgreplay.</li>
    <li>Choose <strong>Refresh</strong> on its page, which fetches the new tools.</li>
    <li>Start a new chat.</li>
  </ol>
  {chatgptDirectory.listed && (
    <p>If you added {chatgptDirectory.name} from the Plugin Directory, it updates on its own; you don't need to refresh it.</p>
  )}
  <h3>Claude Code</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Type <code>/mcp</code>.</li>
    <li>Choose tcgreplay and <strong>Reconnect</strong>, and authenticate again if asked.</li>
    <li>If the tool still doesn't appear, quit and restart Claude Code.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Next</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="/docs/sign-in">Signing in and opening the board</a>: what to expect from Google, and how to open the board
      link.
    </li>
    <li><a href="/docs/workflows">Coaching workflows</a>: what to ask once you're connected.</li>
  </ul>
</Docs>
